HOW TO READ THIS
  Q1  worstLinRes <= ~1e-9      -> the inner solves are NOT the precision limit,
                                   and audit.md section 1's clearing of TD-003 stands.
  Q2  fuel bal falling with     -> the 4.33% is a STOPPING-CRITERION artefact; the
      march length                 gate should require steadiness.
      fuel bal plateauing       -> a REAL conservation defect; no march length fixes
                                   it and TD-004 must repair the discretisation.
  Q3  e/f staying at ~1.0000    -> the two balances are ONE measurement (F12), and
                                   the gate must not count them as two.

=================================================================================================
CORRECTION TO THIS LOG'S COLUMN HEADER (added after the run; the DATA is valid and unaltered)
=================================================================================================
The probe's header string was not updated when the `energy bal` column was dropped from the row,
so the printed header is one column wider than the data and the labels after `fuel bal` are
shifted. The numbers are correct; only the labels are misaligned. The true mapping, read from the
printf argument list in tools/balance_probe.cpp, is:

  relaxT  marchSteps  steady  dT_resid    fuel_bal      e/f      |sumY-1|   S_L    x_front  T_peak   offCells  recentr
    10.0        3968      no  1.6619e-01  4.327958e-02  1.00002  6.2910e-07 4.86230  3.50000  1800.00     47.50      920
    30.0       11905      no  3.7687e-01  6.343790e-01  1.00000  1.0996e-06 4.86230  3.50000  1800.00    163.96     8857
    90.0       35717      no  3.7687e-01  6.343790e-01  1.00000  1.1035e-06 4.86230  3.50000  1800.00    163.96    32669

  x_front in mm (anchor = 3.50 mm, domain 10 mm); T_peak in K (T_ad = 1800); offCells = worst
  front offset from the anchor during the march, in cells; recentr = recentrings during the march.

The header string in the probe source is fixed, so a future run prints correctly. This log is
annotated rather than re-run: the measurement cost ~21 minutes and the data needs no repeat.
